\":\"What to Annotate 1 (Specific Disease); What NOT to Annotate 4 (cancer retained)\"},{\"id\":2,\"entity\":\"CompositeMention\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"breast and ovarian cancers\\\" is a contiguous string referring to two separate diseases (breast cancer and ovarian cancer), so it is annotated as one Composite Mention rather than split, since splitting would lose information.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 2 (Composite Mention); Examples 7\"},{\"id\":3,\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"cancer\\\" in \\\"cancer-causing deletion\\\" is a disease mention used as a modifier of the noun \\\"deletion,\\\" so it is annotated as a Modifier rather than a standalone disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 3 (Modifier); What NOT to Annotate 4 (cancer retained)\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4085, "output_tokens": 1633, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1203}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}